# Keep the build context small and secret-free.
# The server's .env is the one exception: the Dockerfile bind-mounts the context for a single
# RUN step and copies ONLY its NEXT_PUBLIC_* lines (public by definition) into the build. It is
# never COPY'd, so no secret lands in an image layer. It is still part of the build context, which
# BuildKit can keep in the build host's cache: run `docker builder prune -f` after a build.
.env*
!.env
node_modules
.next
.git
.gitignore
data
test-results
playwright-report
tests
marketing
docs
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
*.md
